Third-party notices for phasekit
================================

phasekit is a from-scratch Rust implementation. Its fluid data, and the
algorithms it re-implements, derive from CoolProp v8.0.0 (commit ae81610e),
which is distributed under the MIT License below. The design documents in
docs/ quote and cite CoolProp source locations for the same reason.

The superancillary (saturation-curve) coefficients in CoolProp's fluid files
were fitted by NIST's fastchebpure (https://github.com/usnistgov/fastchebpure),
the code accompanying "Superancillary Equations for the Multiparameter
Equations of State in REFPROP 10.0" (I. H. Bell, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 53,
2024, doi:10.1063/5.0191228). phasekit ships them under CoolProp's MIT
notice and credits NIST and fastchebpure for them. phasekit's superancillary
evaluation (crates/phasekit-core/src/saturation.rs: the Clenshaw order and the
mapping of each piece to [-1, 1]) follows CoolProp's
include/CoolProp/superancillary/superancillary.h, which carries the NIST
notice reproduced at the end of this file.

GERG-2008's coefficients (O. Kunz and W. Wagner, J. Chem. Eng. Data 57 (2012)
3032, doi:10.1021/je300655b) are transcribed from NIST's AGA8 code
(https://github.com/usnistgov/AGA8, commit 3bdb9ab8) into
crates/phasekit-mix/src/gerg/tables.rs, and its test data and values computed
with NIST's teqp 0.23.2 (https://github.com/usnistgov/teqp) are among
phasekit's test fixtures. phasekit credits NIST, AGA8 and teqp for them; both
carry the NIST notice reproduced at the end of this file (and in
LICENSES/LicenseRef-NIST-GERG.txt).

The lane expm1 of phasekit-core's `simd` feature
(crates/phasekit-core/src/num/lanes/) is a port of the libm crate's
(https://github.com/rust-lang/compiler-builtins, MIT), which ported FreeBSD's
msun; its MIT notice and Sun Microsystems' notice are reproduced below.

phasekit-core's own exp, ln and pow (crates/phasekit-core/src/num/elementary/)
are ports of Arm's optimized-routines
(https://github.com/ARM-software/optimized-routines, MIT OR Apache-2.0 WITH
LLVM-exception), whose MIT notice is reproduced below.

phasekit is not affiliated with or endorsed by the CoolProp project or NIST.

